From: TheMoon <execorvo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tcp: make BBR the active default congestion control

CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BBR=y only compiles BBR in as an available option;
without CONFIG_DEFAULT_BBR=y the kernel keeps using whatever the
Kconfig default congestion-control choice resolves to (typically
cubic), so BBR sat unused unless userspace flipped
net.ipv4.tcp_congestion_control manually at boot. This makes BBR the
actual default from boot.

Applies to: kernel-6.6/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index 4e687735adeb..2222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -159,6 +158,7 @@ CONFIG_TCP_CONG_ADVANCED=y
 # CONFIG_TCP_CONG_WESTWOOD is not set
 # CONFIG_TCP_CONG_HTCP is not set
 CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BBR=y
+CONFIG_DEFAULT_BBR=y
 CONFIG_IPV6_ROUTER_PREF=y
 CONFIG_IPV6_ROUTE_INFO=y
 CONFIG_IPV6_OPTIMISTIC_DAD=y
